„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections—…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbWoe to Ariel, to Ariel, the city where David dwelt! add ye year to year; let them kill sacrifices.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeYet I will distress Ariel, and there shall be heaviness and sorrow: and it shall be unto me as Ariel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|And I will camp against thee round about, and will lay siege against thee with a mount, and I will raise forts against thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙïAnd thou shalt be brought down, and shalt speak out of the ground, and thy speech shall be low out of the dust, and thy voice shall be, as of one that hath a familiar spirit, out of the ground, and thy speech shall whisper out of the dust.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶Moreover the multitude of thy strangers shall be like small dust, and the multitude of the terrible ones shall be as chaff that passeth away: yea, it shall be at an instant suddenly.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—Thou shalt be visited of the LORD of hosts with thunder, and with earthquake, and great noise, with storm and tempest, and the flame of devouring fire.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®And the multitude of all the nations that fight against Ariel, even all that fight against her and her munition, and that distress her, shall be as a dream of a night vision.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ?It shall even be as when an hungry man dreameth, and, behold, he eateth; but he awaketh, and his soul is empty: or as when a thirsty man dreameth, and, behold, he drinketh; but he awaketh, and, behold, he is faint, and his soul hath appetite: so shall the multitude of all the nations be, that fight against mount Zion.¦layout ª