„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃAnd the vision of all is become unto you as the words of a book that is sealed, which men deliver to one that is learned, saying, Read this, I pray thee: and he saith, I cannot; for it is sealed:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuand the book is delivered to him that is not learned, saying, Read this, I pray thee: and he saith, I am not learned.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖWherefore the Lord said, Forasmuch as this people draw near me with their mouth, and with their lips do honour me, but have removed their heart far from me, and their fear toward me is taught by the precept of men:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÙtherefore, behold, I will proceed to do a marvellous work among this people, even a marvellous work and a wonder: for the wisdom of their wise men shall perish, and the understanding of their prudent men shall be hid.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’Woe unto them that seek deep to hide their counsel from the LORD, and their works are in the dark, and they say, Who seeth us? and who knoweth us?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÛSurely your turning of things upside down shall be esteemed as the potter's clay: for shall the work say of him that made it, He made me not? or shall the thing framed say of him that framed it, He had no understanding?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹Is it not yet a very little while, and Lebanon shall be turned into a fruitful field, and the fruitful field shall be esteemed as a forest?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…And in that day shall the deaf hear the words of the book, and the eyes of the blind shall see out of obscurity, and out of darkness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsThe meek also shall increase their joy in the LORD, and the poor among men shall rejoice in the Holy One of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtFor the terrible one is brought to nought, and the scorner is consumed, and all that watch for iniquity are cut off:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠthat make a man an offender for a word, and lay a snare for him that reproveth in the gate, and turn aside the just for a thing of nought.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜Therefore thus saith the LORD, who redeemed Abraham, concerning the house of Jacob, Jacob shall not now be ashamed, neither shall his face now wax pale.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¯But when he seeth his children, the work of mine hands, in the midst of him, they shall sanctify my name, and sanctify the Holy One of Jacob, and shall fear the God of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhThey also that erred in spirit shall come to understanding, and they that murmured shall learn doctrine.¦layout ªlast_verse